* =============================================================
* MQSC commands to configure QMGRNATIVEHA for the tcp-to-mq ACE flow
* Queue Manager: qmgr-native-ha in namespace cp4i-mq
*
* To apply:
*   oc exec -n cp4i-mq qmgr-native-ha-ibm-mq-0 -- \
*     runmqsc QMGRNATIVEHA < demo-pre-reqs/mq/queues.mqsc
* =============================================================

* ─── CONNAUTH: disable client credential checking ────────────────────────────
* IBM MQ on OpenShift runs with an arbitrary UID (e.g. 1000890000) that has
* no corresponding named OS user. Setting MCAUSER to any named user triggers
* AMQ9557E (user ID init failure). CHCKCLNT(NONE) is safe here because the
* channel is internal-cluster-only (no SSL, no external exposure).
ALTER AUTHINFO(SYSTEM.DEFAULT.AUTHINFO.IDPWOS) AUTHTYPE(IDPWOS) CHCKCLNT(NONE)
REFRESH SECURITY TYPE(CONNAUTH)

* ─── Channel for ACE client connections (no SSL for internal cluster use) ────
* MCAUSER left blank: MQ uses the queue manager process user for OAM checks.
* Do NOT set MCAUSER to a named user on OpenShift — MQ cannot initialize
* named users (AMQ9557E) when they don't exist in the pod's /etc/passwd.
DEFINE CHANNEL('ACE.SVRCONN') CHLTYPE(SVRCONN) TRPTYPE(TCP) MCAUSER('') REPLACE

* Allow all users except 'nobody'
SET CHLAUTH('ACE.SVRCONN') TYPE(BLOCKUSER) USERLIST('nobody')

* ─── Input queue: receives messages from the TCP/IP ACE flow ─────────────────
DEFINE QLOCAL('CP4I.DEMO.IN.Q') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE

* ─── Output queue: for the MQ-to-MQ transform flow (future use) ──────────────
DEFINE QLOCAL('CP4I.DEMO.OUT.Q') DEFPSIST(YES) MAXDEPTH(5000) REPLACE

* ─── Auth records: grant mqm user access ─────────────────────────────────────
SET AUTHREC OBJTYPE(QMGR) PRINCIPAL('mqm') AUTHADD(CONNECT,INQ)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('CP4I.DEMO.IN.Q') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('mqm') AUTHADD(PUT,GET,INQ,BROWSE)
SET AUTHREC PROFILE('CP4I.DEMO.OUT.Q') OBJTYPE(QUEUE) PRINCIPAL('mqm') AUTHADD(PUT,GET,INQ,BROWSE)
